Z||000003||ray b||08-23-2001||11:50 PM||||4.0 is a olds motor, i wonder if they are having a going out of bizz sale??<BR>is it a shortblock, long block, ornew/rebuilt ready to run motor??or take out junk motor??<BR>you will need a wiring harness pluss computer chips/socket stock or after market,<BR>and all acc for motor including intake and exhaust manafolds<BR>but it will bolt up to the trans in your car!!<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||08-24-2001||11:47 AM||||Anything is possible :)<P>The 4.0L is the Aurora V8 version of the northstar.<P>It's not a simple swap, but the engine *does* bolt up to fiero trannys.....<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><BR> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by jeffndebrus:<BR><B>I recently aquired a 1985 se 2.8 v6 with auto trans.  Tonight I found two 4.0l 32 valve engines in crates.  They do not have transmissions with them.  Please tell me what options I have here.  My mechanical experience is limited.  But the thought of it inspires me.  Any advice would be helpful&gt; Thank you!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
